<title>TURKEY: Turk Tofas to give bonus, pay dividend.</title>
<headline>Turk Tofas to give bonus, pay dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's leading car maker Tofas Turk Otomobil Fabrikasi A.S., owned jointly by Koc Holding and Italy's Fiat SpA, said it would raise its capital to 12.6 trillion lira from 8.4 trillion.</p>
<p>It will issue 0.5 bonus and pay 143 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from May 30, Tofas said in a statement.</p>
<p>Most of the bonus issue totalling 4.2 trillion lira will be met by revalued company funds and 400 billion lira of it by additional dividends which will be retained.</p>
<p>The cash dividend will total 1.2 trillion lira, to be distributed from 1996 net profits of 4.6 trillion lira.</p>
<p>Koc Holding and Fiat each hold a 37.86 percent stake in Tofas.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
